# Unity Editor Agent (compile + Edit Mode tests + editor actions)

Grid Dungeon uses [`com.miraluna.editor-agent`](../../com.miraluna.editor-agent) for structured **compile**, **Edit Mode test**, and **editor action** checks while the Editor stays open.

Authority: [tools/README.md](../../griddungeon-game/tools/README.md), package [README.md](../../com.miraluna.editor-agent/README.md).

## When to run (agents)

After handoff-touching **`.cs`** changes when the Unity Editor **may be open** on `griddungeon-game`:

```powershell
cd <griddungeon-game>
.\tools\request-compile-status.ps1
```

After **test** changes (or before closing a test ticket), when Editor may be open — follow **editor-agent-test** skill:

```powershell
.\tools\request-test-status.ps1 -Category <Domain>
# or
.\tools\request-agent.ps1 -Action Test -Category Combat
```

After **scene/content regen** or when user asks to **run/list agent tools** — follow **editor-agent-action** skill:

```powershell
.\tools\list-agent-tools.ps1
.\tools\request-action-status.ps1 -ToolName create-dev-bootstrap
# or
.\tools\request-agent.ps1 -Action Invoke -ToolName ensure-content-database
```

- Compile exit **0** required before claiming compile-clean.
- Test exit **0** before claiming Edit Mode tests green (when you ran them).
- Exit **1** — fix errors/failures; re-run until green.
- Exit **2** — timeout; confirm Editor is open and package resolved.
- Exit **3** — Editor did not claim request; open project in Unity.

Do **not** run `tools/ci-compile.ps1` or `Unity.exe -batchmode -runTests` while the Editor has this project open. See `unity-no-cli-tests-while-editor-open.mdc`.

## Fallbacks

| Situation | Command |
|-----------|---------|
| Read last compile JSON only | `.\tools\read-compile-status.ps1` |
| Read last test JSON only | `.\tools\read-test-status.ps1` |
| Read last action JSON only | `.\tools\read-action-status.ps1` |
| Package/JSON unavailable | `.\tools\read-unity-editor-log.ps1` |
| Editor closed — compile | `.\tools\ci-compile.ps1` |
| Editor closed — tests | `Unity.exe -runTests -testPlatform editmode` |

## Output

| File | Content |
|------|---------|
| `Logs/last-compile.json` | `file`, `line`, `column`, `message` |
| `Logs/last-test.json` | `summary`, `failures[]` |
| `Logs/last-action.json` | `ok`, `toolName`, `message`, `createdAssetPaths`, `error` |

Unity menu: **Tools → Miraluna → Request Compile Status** / **Request Test Run**.

## Other projects

Install the same UPM package via `manifest.json`, copy/wrap `tools/*.ps1`, add equivalent cursor rules.
